# Fixed-width subtype insertion rejects a scaled literal overflow

Verifies an insertion applies the same scaled conversion as an array literal:
`13cm` must become `130mm` before it enters `int8<mm>[]` storage, and that
magnitude does not fit `int8`, so the insertion is rejected while compiling.

>>> source
let sizes: int8<mm>[] = []
sizes->push(13cm)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: array element `int8[cm]` cannot be represented as `int8[mm]` at Span { start: 39, end: 43 }

<<< exit
1
